<%= header_section(@subject) %>
<div>
  <p>
    The site can put the page back between about <strong><%= @window_starts_on.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %></strong> and
    <strong><%= @window_ends_on.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %></strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    To stop that, file a court action against the person who posted the page before then, and reply to this email to
    tell us. If you do nothing, the site can put the page back.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What happened:</strong> the person who posted the page sent the site a counter-notice on
    <%= @report.counter_notice_received_on.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %>. A counter-notice says they have the right to
    share the work. The law lets the site put the page back 10 to 14 business days after it got the counter-notice.
    The full counter-notice is below.
  </p>
  <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><%= @report.counter_notice_body %></pre>
  <p>
    <%= link_to "View your report", @report_url, class: "button primary" %>
  </p>
</div>
